    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "109a3f65-f069-32d8-a525-66c866b2c0c8",
                "word": "Dorcas",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "de1f9f0d-8628-330b-b3dc-a513adedf991",
                        "entry_id": "109a3f65-f069-32d8-a525-66c866b2c0c8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A woman who is said, in the Bible, to have been restored to life by Peter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea765e84-a81e-44e6-9d49-62b213ed847f",
                                "sense_id": "de1f9f0d-8628-330b-b3dc-a513adedf991",
                                "text": "Now there was at Joppa a certain disciple named Tabitha, which by interpretation is called Dorcas; this woman was full of good works and almsdeeds which she did."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cb48a7af-499f-3a15-824c-0c8b67cf382f",
                        "entry_id": "109a3f65-f069-32d8-a525-66c866b2c0c8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A female given name from Ancient Greek of biblical origin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2434d2b0-9392-31d1-bfdc-60b3f16e7eb7",
                        "entry_id": "109a3f65-f069-32d8-a525-66c866b2c0c8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Used attributively of a ladies' association within the church in order to make and distribute clothes for the poor."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "attributive",
                            "form-of",
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "518ea1a9-6156-4c6e-b6fa-48e9a9091ec5",
                                "sense_id": "2434d2b0-9392-31d1-bfdc-60b3f16e7eb7",
                                "text": "She established a Dorcas society at Baslehurst, of which she became permanent president, and spent her money in carrying on this institution in the manner most pleasing to herself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "58c56454-4caa-4bf5-988b-10c3420f9c9f",
                                "sense_id": "2434d2b0-9392-31d1-bfdc-60b3f16e7eb7",
                                "text": "The daughter was probably some prim Miss, neat, sensible, pious, but all in a small feminine way, in which Felix was no more interested than in Dorcas meetings, biographies of devout women, and that amount of ornamental knitting which was not inconsistent with Nonconforming seriousness."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "6886a423-1682-3132-a593-5e54743b2741",
                "word": "Dorcas",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f107e236-0ed4-4bd4-8ae7-08a2bdadceca",
                        "entry_id": "6886a423-1682-3132-a593-5e54743b2741",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Dorcasses"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "dd11f0f5-a430-4c7e-ae87-75e5d645f54a",
                        "entry_id": "6886a423-1682-3132-a593-5e54743b2741",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Dorcases"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ffeffd80-e0c9-3bc1-a441-b63f6bf58da1",
                        "entry_id": "6886a423-1682-3132-a593-5e54743b2741",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A member of a Dorcas association."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "61ce13aa-3c79-4d77-832b-019b283d394f",
                                "sense_id": "ffeffd80-e0c9-3bc1-a441-b63f6bf58da1",
                                "text": "Secondly, When a person not only hath grace, but also is beneficial, usefull, doth much good in his time, is diffusive of holinesse, full of good works, serves his generation, and hath done his work before he fals asleep, hath his Dorcasses coats to be seen after his death; it is only our doing good that makes us called good;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe883bc2-7fda-41ec-97c9-2aff3fc38528",
                                "sense_id": "ffeffd80-e0c9-3bc1-a441-b63f6bf58da1",
                                "text": "I have beheld, O Dorcasses! with admiration and gratitude , the coats and garments, the lint and bandages which you have made."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b383470e-ebac-44fe-aa21-0ef66dd734e4",
                                "sense_id": "ffeffd80-e0c9-3bc1-a441-b63f6bf58da1",
                                "text": "yea, of women, not a few, who following in the train of those who “ministered to Christ,” were good Dorcasses, and “succourers of many.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0b61b03-a895-470b-89e4-e806a1388346",
                                "sense_id": "ffeffd80-e0c9-3bc1-a441-b63f6bf58da1",
                                "text": "I fear least thro the medium of the papers he shᵈ hear of it before the Dorcasses of his congregation shall receive the certificate to present in due form, in this case be pleased to apologize to the ladies for my indiscretion."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
